---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { site } from '@/data/site';

const emailHref = `mailto:${site.email}?subject=${encodeURIComponent('Website terms question')}`;
---
<BaseLayout
  meta={{
    title: 'Website Terms — Raju Das Rudro',
    description: 'Public website terms covering use of the Raju Das Rudro portfolio, service information, insights and project inquiry features.',
    pathname: '/terms/',
  }}
>
  <article class="section legal-page">
    <div class="container reading legal-content">
      <header class="legal-header">
        <p class="eyebrow">Website Information</p>
        <h1>Website Terms</h1>
        <p class="lede">These Terms explain the conditions for using this public personal-brand website. They are website terms only and do not replace a project-specific services agreement.</p>
      </header>

      <section aria-labelledby="terms-introduction">
        <h2 id="terms-introduction">Introduction and Use of the Website</h2>
        <p>This website is operated as the professional personal-brand website of Raju Das Rudro. By using the site, you are using it subject to these public Website Terms and the functionality made available here.</p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="terms-purpose">
        <h2 id="terms-purpose">Website Purpose</h2>
        <p>The website presents work, service information, professional insights and ways to make a project inquiry. Website content is general information and may be updated as services, examples or site functionality change.</p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="terms-inquiries">
        <h2 id="terms-inquiries">Service and Project Inquiries</h2>
        <p>Submitting a project inquiry expresses interest and allows a potential project to be discussed. An inquiry is not an order, binding quote or automatic service agreement.</p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="terms-acceptance">
        <h2 id="terms-acceptance">No Automatic Project Acceptance</h2>
        <p>Submitting an inquiry does not mean the project has been accepted. Any project acceptance or commitment should be confirmed separately through the appropriate communication or project-specific agreement.</p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="terms-scope">
        <h2 id="terms-scope">Project Scope</h2>
        <p>For an accepted project, deliverables, scope, responsibilities, revisions where relevant, payment, schedule and ownership or licensing terms should be agreed separately. These Website Terms do not create universal project terms for every engagement.</p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="terms-pricing">
        <h2 id="terms-pricing">Pricing and Timeline</h2>
        <p>Budget and timeline choices shown in the Contact form are optional inquiry context only. They are not fixed public pricing, a guaranteed start date, a guaranteed delivery period or an automatically accepted quote. Final pricing and schedule are confirmed separately for an accepted project.</p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="terms-ip">
        <h2 id="terms-ip">Intellectual Property and Site Content</h2>
        <p>Original website text, Raju Das Rudro branding, site-created layouts, design presentation and original site assets are presented as part of this website. Client-owned materials, third-party logos, marketplace assets and other external materials remain subject to their respective rights and permissions.</p>
        <p>Ownership and usage rights for commissioned client work are determined separately by the applicable project agreement, order or platform terms rather than by this public page.</p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="terms-use">
        <h2 id="terms-use">Acceptable Website Use</h2>
        <p>Please do not interfere with website operation, misuse the Contact mechanism, attempt abusive automated submissions, or falsely represent an association with Raju Das Rudro through use of the site.</p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="terms-third-party">
        <h2 id="terms-third-party">Third-Party Links</h2>
        <p>The site may link to external destinations such as Fiverr. Those services are operated independently and are governed by their own terms, policies and service conditions. This website does not control those external services.</p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="terms-outcomes">
        <h2 id="terms-outcomes">No Guaranteed Business or Marketing Outcomes</h2>
        <p>Service descriptions, portfolio examples and educational content do not guarantee sales, conversions, revenue, traffic, search rankings, campaign performance or other business outcomes. Results vary by project, market, execution and other factors, and any project-specific commitments must be agreed separately.</p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="terms-availability">
        <h2 id="terms-availability">Website Availability and Changes</h2>
        <p>Website content and features may be changed, corrected or updated. Availability may occasionally be interrupted, and constant or error-free access is not promised.</p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="terms-disclaimer">
        <h2 id="terms-disclaimer">Website-Level Disclaimer and Limitation</h2>
        <p>The site is provided for general professional and business information. Reasonable care is taken with published content, but general website information should not be treated as a project-specific commitment. Project-specific responsibilities and remedies, where applicable, should be established separately.</p>
        <p>More detailed contractual limitations, if needed for future client agreements, should be reviewed separately rather than assumed from these Website Terms.</p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="terms-changes">
        <h2 id="terms-changes">Changes to These Terms</h2>
        <p>These public Website Terms may be updated when the website, business practices or relevant requirements change. No amendment history is implied unless one is expressly published.</p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="terms-contact">
        <h2 id="terms-contact">Contact</h2>
        <p>Questions about these Website Terms can be sent to <a href={emailHref}>{site.email}</a>.</p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
.legal-page{padding-top:var(--space-10)}
.legal-content{display:grid;gap:var(--space-8);margin-inline:auto}
.legal-header{display:grid;gap:var(--space-4);padding-bottom:var(--space-6);border-bottom:1px solid var(--color-border)}
.legal-header h1{max-width:14ch}
.legal-header .lede{max-width:42rem}
.legal-content section{display:grid;gap:var(--space-3)}
.legal-content h2{font-size:clamp(1.35rem,2vw,1.75rem)}
.legal-content p,.legal-content li{color:#475569;font-size:var(--fs-body);line-height:var(--lh-body)}
.legal-content ul{display:grid;gap:.45rem;padding-left:1.25rem}
.legal-content a{color:#174ea6;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-thickness:1px;text-underline-offset:3px;overflow-wrap:anywhere}
@media(max-width:47.99rem){.legal-page{padding-top:var(--space-8)}.legal-content{gap:var(--space-6)}.legal-header{padding-bottom:var(--space-5)}}
</style>
